    primaryTypology: 'educational',
    signatureMaterial: 'brick',
    portrait: {
      en: 'The founder of modern architecture in Bangladesh, and the man who decided the country should not build it alone. Trained in Dhaka, Oregon and at the Architectural Association, Islam returned in the 1950s and set the terms with the Faculty of Fine Arts at Dhaka University: brick, deep verandahs, a plan that runs with the monsoon rather than against it. He then used his standing to bring Louis Kahn, Paul Rudolph, Richard Neutra, Stanley Tigerman and Constantinos Doxiadis to work in East Pakistan — it was Islam who steered the National Assembly commission to Kahn rather than keep it. His own campuses at Chittagong and Jahangirnagar step down their hillsides in staggered terraces. He was also a political activist, and his work is on Bangladesh’s World Heritage tentative list.',
      es: 'Fundador de la arquitectura moderna en Bangladesh y el hombre que decidió que el país no debía construirla solo. Formado en Dacca, Oregón y la Architectural Association, Islam volvió en los años cincuenta y fijó las reglas con la Facultad de Bellas Artes de la Universidad de Dacca: ladrillo, galerías profundas, una planta que corre a favor del monzón y no en su contra. Usó luego su prestigio para traer a Louis Kahn, Paul Rudolph, Richard Neutra, Stanley Tigerman y Constantinos Doxiadis a trabajar en Pakistán Oriental —fue él quien derivó a Kahn el encargo de la Asamblea Nacional en lugar de quedárselo—. Sus campus de Chittagong y Jahangirnagar bajan por la ladera en terrazas escalonadas. Fue también activista político, y su obra figura en la lista indicativa de Patrimonio Mundial de Bangladesh.',
      it: 'Il fondatore dell’architettura moderna in Bangladesh, e l’uomo che decise che il paese non dovesse costruirla da solo. Formatosi a Dacca, in Oregon e alla Architectural Association, Islam tornò negli anni Cinquanta e fissò le regole con la Facoltà di Belle Arti dell’Università di Dacca: mattone, verande profonde, una pianta che asseconda il monsone invece di contrastarlo. Usò poi il proprio prestigio per portare Louis Kahn, Paul Rudolph, Richard Neutra, Stanley Tigerman e Constantinos Doxiadis a lavorare nel Pakistan orientale — fu lui a dirottare su Kahn la commessa dell’Assemblea nazionale anziché tenerla. I suoi campus di Chittagong e Jahangirnagar scendono lungo il pendio in terrazze sfalsate. Fu anche attivista politico, e la sua opera figura nella lista propositiva del Patrimonio Mondiale del Bangladesh.',
    },
    awards: ['Independence Day Award (1999)', 'Ekushey Padak (1972)'],
    tier: 'canon',
    context: null,
